<title>JAPAN: Nintendo jumps on good game machine sales.</title>
<headline>Nintendo jumps on good game machine sales.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nintendo Co Ltd jumped in Thursday afternoon trade, encouraged by good sales of the game maker's new N64 video game machines in the United States, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price was up 80 yen at 7,410 yen at 0523 GMT, on a volume of 217,900 shares.  </p>
<p>On Wednesday, the U.S. unit of Nintendo said in a statement that its entire shipment of N64 video game machines, totalling 350,000 units, sold out at retail stores three days after their launch.</p>
<p>Nintendo told Reuters on Thursday that it was considering boosting shipments of the players to the United States in view of their popularity there.</p>
</text>
